### Sample 09 - Azure Service Bus
###
### Prerequisites: infra\provision.ps1 has been run, the Publisher is listening on
### http://localhost:5009, and the Consumer is running in another terminal.
###
### NOTE: some HTTP clients built on .NET's HttpClient (including the Visual Studio .http runner)
### append their own traceparent header. See sample 08 for why that matters.

@publisher = http://localhost:5009

### Index - confirms which namespace and queue this instance is wired to.
GET {{publisher}}/

### Health probe.
GET {{publisher}}/health

### 1. Place an order.
### The order row and its outbox record commit together in one local SQL transaction. Nothing has
### reached Service Bus yet. Copy "outboxId" from the response into @outboxId below.
POST {{publisher}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "dnv-maritime",
  "customerId": "cust-9001",
  "total": 1499.50
}

### Paste the outboxId from the response above.
@outboxId = 01A1C992-7F6A-7003-A69E-45280DCED616

### 2. Inspect the record. Within a few seconds status becomes "Delivered" and attemptCount is 1.
GET {{publisher}}/outbox/{{outboxId}}

### 3. Resend the SAME record. This replays the identical MessageId, which is exactly what the
### dispatcher does when a send succeeds but its acknowledgement is lost.
###
### Watch the Consumer terminal: it does NOT print a second RECEIVED block. The broker accepted
### the message and silently discarded it, because duplicate detection is keyed on MessageId and
### the window is 10 minutes.
POST {{publisher}}/outbox/{{outboxId}}/resend

### 4. Run it again. Still no new message at the consumer.
POST {{publisher}}/outbox/{{outboxId}}/resend

### 5. Place a different order to prove the queue is still live and the consumer is not stuck.
### This one has a new outbox id, so it is not a duplicate and it arrives immediately.
POST {{publisher}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "dnv-energy",
  "customerId": "cust-9002",
  "total": 275.00
}

### 6. Counters. delivered should equal the number of orders placed - resends do not create records.
GET {{publisher}}/outbox/stats
